      "hints": [
        "Apply the binomial expansion $\\binom{5}{r}3^{5-r}(-2x)^r$ to find the first three terms of $(3 - 2x)^5$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Expand $(3 - 2x)^5$ in ascending powers of $x$ up to $x^2$ using the binomial theorem:\n$$(3 - 2x)^5 = \\binom{5}{0}3^5 + \\binom{5}{1}3^4(-2x) + \\binom{5}{2}3^3(-2x)^2 + \\dots$$",
        "Evaluate each term:\n$$= 243 + 5(81)(-2x) + 10(27)(4x^2) = 243 - 810x + 1080x^2$$"
      ],
